es_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Discord username (optional)\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Describe the bug\r\n\r\nPossibly related to #61\r\n\r\nIn both macOS Terminal and iTerm I can use my system clipboard independently from the terminal clipboard.\r\nCTRL+W seems to interfere with this.  In Warp, CTRL+W also copies the cut text into my system clipboard.  In addition, it does not seem to update the terminal clipboard.\r\n\r\n\r\n### To Reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Write `testing1 testing2 testing3`\r\n2. CTRL+U - cuts the line\r\n3. CTRL+Y - pastes `testing1 testing2 testing3`\r\n4. CTRL+W - cuts `testing3`\r\n5. CTRL+Y - pastes `testing1 testing2 testing3` - WRONG\r\n\r\nfinal result is\r\n`testing1 testing2 testing1 testing2 testing3`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behaviour\r\n\r\nI expected the final output to be `testing1 testing2 testing3`, as the final word cut and pasted was `testing3`\r\n\r\nAdditional:\r\nAs a side effect, the system clipboard is now also `testing1 testing2 testing1 testing2 testing3`. IMO none of these commands should interfere with system clipboard, unless you deem it a \"feature\" of Warp (TIHI)\r\n\r\n### Screenshots\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Operating System\r\n\r\nMacOS\r\n\r\n### OS Version\r\n\r\n2.6\r\n\r\n### Shell Version\r\n\r\nzsh 5.8.1\r\n\r\n### Warp Version\r\n\r\nv0.2022.09.27.08.11.stable_00\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Does this block you from using Warp daily?\r\n\r\nNo\r\n\r\n### Warp Internal (ignore): linear-label:b8107fdf-ba31-488d-b103-d271c89cac3e\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"dannyneira","id":16809145,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODA5MTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16809145?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dannyneira","html_url":"https://github.com/dannyneira","followers_url":"https://api.g